    {
      "id": 3,
      "kind": "F_retrieval",
      "payload": "{\"characters\":0,\"documents\":[],\"llm_tokens\":0,\"query\":\"A locality SIMD OpenMP\"}",
      "created": 1792255450.9583697
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Parallel-kernel lane: evaluate row-wise OpenMP on the ARM64 four-core target, using a race-free OR reduction for the convergence flag and strict barriers between reading the current grid and writing/copying or swapping it. Compare ordinary parallel loops, a persistent team, and a serial cutoff because the valid baseline is only 0.06897 s. Preserve the actual strict `error > 1e-5`, iteration bound, operand order, and Jacobi (not in-place/red-black) semantics.\",\"B\":\"Memory/dataflow lane: investigate contiguous allocation, alias-friendly indexing, and removal of the second interior sweep via ping-pong buffers. A swap implementation must keep the original boundary values in both buffers: the baseline never updates boundary cells, including when the initial hot region touches them. Preserve the live-buffer output and validate tiny grids, zero iterations, and all iteration parities; do not use numerical shortcuts.\",\"C\":\"I/O and control-overhead lane: determine whether `%lf` serialization or iteration bookkeeping dominates this short benchmark. Test only behavior-preserving buffering/locking/batching approaches that retain row-major output, six-decimal `%lf` behavior, trailing spaces, and newlines. Also assess safe convergence-flag overhead reductions without omitting any stencil calculation. Reject custom formatting or convergence prediction unless equivalence holds for general valid inputs.\",\"G\":\"Integration lane: independently validate and benchmark every tree result, then only combine compatible changes after measuring the combined program. Use the unchanged environment and all available correctness cases; retain the baseline as fallback. Compare repeated timings against the 0.06897 s valid baseline, account for noise and parallel/I/O overhead, and select the fastest valid result rather than assuming gains are additive.\",\"analysis\":\"The only measurement is a valid four-case baseline on four-core ARM64: 0.06897 s mean (0.06815–0.07040 s). The executable performs two interior sweeps per iteration, continues when any cell has a strictly greater-than-threshold change, leaves boundaries unchanged, and prints every cell serially. Thus promising general-purpose avenues are parallel row work, reducing memory traffic with correctly bounded ping-pong storage, and output overhead; changing stopping behavior, using an in-place recurrence, or specializing inputs would violate correctness.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"e318ad6b1fc029d8c5f7fa13ce6c4238f4ec607682859d429b769d06e5a6c143\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Parallel-kernel lane: evaluate row-wise OpenMP on the ARM64 four-core target, using a race-free OR reduction for the convergence flag and strict barriers between reading the current grid and writing/copying or swapping it. Compare ordinary parallel loops, a persistent team, and a serial cutoff because the valid baseline is only 0.06897 s. Preserve the actual strict `error > 1e-5`, iteration bound, operand order, and Jacobi (not in-place/red-black) semantics.\",\"B\":\"Memory/dataflow lane: investigate contiguous allocation, alias-friendly indexing, and removal of the second interior sweep via ping-pong buffers. A swap implementation must keep the original boundary values in both buffers: the baseline never updates boundary cells, including when the initial hot region touches them. Preserve the live-buffer output and validate tiny grids, zero iterations, and all iteration parities; do not use numerical shortcuts.\",\"C\":\"I/O and control-overhead lane: determine whether `%lf` serialization or iteration bookkeeping dominates this short benchmark. Test only behavior-preserving buffering/locking/batching approaches that retain row-major output, six-decimal `%lf` behavior, trailing spaces, and newlines. Also assess safe convergence-flag overhead reductions without omitting any stencil calculation. Reject custom formatting or convergence prediction unless equivalence holds for general valid inputs.\",\"G\":\"Integration lane: independently validate and benchmark every tree result, then only combine compatible changes after measuring the combined program. Use the unchanged environment and all available correctness cases; retain the baseline as fallback. Compare repeated timings against the 0.06897 s valid baseline, account for noise and parallel/I/O overhead, and select the fastest valid result rather than assuming gains are additive.\",\"analysis\":\"The only measurement is a valid four-case baseline on four-core ARM64: 0.06897 s mean (0.06815–0.07040 s). The executable performs two interior sweeps per iteration, continues when any cell has a strictly greater-than-threshold change, leaves boundaries unchanged, and prints every cell serially. Thus promising general-purpose avenues are parallel row work, reducing memory traffic with correctly bounded ping-pong storage, and output overhead; changing stopping behavior, using an in-place recurrence, or specializing inputs would violate correctness.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"aa372084a3554dbe820b2ecfac347405\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"e318ad6b1fc029d8c5f7fa13ce6c4238f4ec607682859d429b769d06e5a6c143\",\"session_id\":\"15219a6fd62b4dcb91b395dcd4ae03d5\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"a864938819cc598c4a94befb84593ca86ecf80fab470431813a123c917b72d01\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":11359,\"output_tokens\":5595,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":5121}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":16954,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
